{#-
  Mobile menu (M1 accordion) + sticky pledge bar — structure from
  design-source/partials/nav-drawer.html (v3). Shown under 940px.

  DESIGN: do not edit structure (one sanctioned departure, below). This partial
  is included AFTER </main>, not inside <header>: .drawer and .pledgebar are
  position:fixed overlays and moving them into the header breaks the stacking
  context (v3 README, "Where the nav markup lives"). Each section opens to its
  description and then its dropdown links — ui.js keeps one section open at a
  time via [data-acc] / .pm / .in.

  Mobile fixes (2026-10-17, founder): the export's "Overview" link at the top of
  each section is removed. It pointed at the section's own url, which is
  already the section's FIRST dropdown link (chrome.json), and the desktop menu
  has no Overview. The build fails if a section's first drawer link is ever not
  the section's own url (eleventy.config.js, drawer landing-page guard), so no
  landing page can quietly drop out of the menu. CANVAS-SYNC 171.

  CONTENT: labels, descriptions and links come from _data/chrome.json, the same
  source the header's mega panels read, so the two never drift apart.
-#}
<div class="drawer" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Menu">
  <div class="drawer-hd">{% image "logos/logo-tight-light.png", "uncost.org", "8rem", [160, 320] %}<button class="drawer-x" type="button" aria-label="Close menu" data-drawer-close>&#10005;</button></div>
  {% for item in chrome.nav %}
  <div class="drawer-acc">
    <button type="button" data-acc aria-expanded="false"><span>{{ item.label }}</span><span class="pm" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
    <div class="in">
      <div class="dd-desc">{{ item.desc }}</div>
      {% for link in item.links %}
      <a href="{{ link.url }}"{% if link.external %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ link.label }}{% if link.badge %}<span class="plan">{{ link.badge }}</span>{% endif %}<span class="ar" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="drawer-sub">{% for link in chrome.navSecondary %}<a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.label }}</a>{% endfor %}</div>
</div>
<div class="pledgebar"><a href="/pledge/">Sign the Pledge</a></div>
